格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DSH plugin: Codex-style computer use for Windows - read the screen, drive mouse & keyboard via SendInput; pairs with picturereader to close the look-act-verify loop.","id":"gh:1341900334","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"computer-user","slug":"jing-hy/computer-user","topics":["computer-use","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","windows"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DSH plugin: Codex-style computer use for Windows - read the screen, drive mouse & keyboard via SendI"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"nput; pairs with picturereader to close the look-act-verify loop."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# computer-user"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**Codex-style computer use for DeepSeek Harness on Windows.**\nThe agent sees the screen, clicks, typ"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"es — or drives named controls through UI Automation. No sidecar, no native build."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"`computer-user` is a DeepSeek Harness bundle that gives an agent\ntwenty-one `computer_*` tools: scre"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"enshot, UI Automation tree, pointer and keyboard input, window control, and a\ntakeover pill with a g"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"lobal stop key that follows you across virtual desktops."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"It ships as a normal DSH plugin — `package.json`, one `cordis.patch.yml`, a settings card, and three"},{"id":"p6s2","text":" PowerShell\nscripts. No native addon, no daemon process, no MCP bridge."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Why this one"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"- **Native DSH bundle, not a bridge.** Tools register through `ctx.tools.register`; settings ride th"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"e 0.2.x\n`SettingsForms` entry; the Web card is a first-class settings section, not a separate page.\n"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"- **Zero native dependencies.** Input uses `SendInput`, capture uses GDI, observation uses UI Automa"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"tion —\nall through Windows PowerShell 5.1 that ships with the OS.\n- **Vision optional.** `computer_s"},{"id":"p8s5","text":"creenshot` returns a PNG path: vision models call `read_image`, text-only\nmodels use picturereader O"},{"id":"p8s6","text":"CR, and `computer_snapshot` acts on named controls without any pixels.\n- **Stops when asked.** A blu"},{"id":"p8s7","text":"e pill appears while the agent has control; the stop key (default `Ctrl+Alt+Esc`)\nor its button writ"},{"id":"p8s8","text":"es a stop flag that every later call refuses to ignore. When a task is done the agent can\nclose the "},{"id":"p8s9","text":"pill itself with `computer_stop` (the approval survives), and the pill follows virtual-desktop switc"},{"id":"p8s10","text":"hes.\n- **Stale-safe.** Element ids are re-resolved on every action, and a screenshot can be fenced o"},{"id":"p8s11","text":"n the\nforeground window — a changed UI fails loudly instead of clicking the wrong thing."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"npm:"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"DSH profile:"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Restart DSH. The tools appear in every session; the card appears under Settings → Computer Use."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"From a checkout:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## The loop"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Coordinate work still works: every input tool takes virtual-screen pixels, and `computer_screenshot`"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"\nreturns `virtual_offset` so multi-monitor rigs line up."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Tools"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Twenty-one tools. `tool_mode` can trim the set to nine everyday ones."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"| Group | Tools |"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"| Observe | `computer_screenshot`, `computer_snapshot`, `computer_list_windows`, `computer_get_curso"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"r_position` |\n| Act with the pointer | `computer_click`, `computer_type`, `computer_keypress`, `comp"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"uter_scroll`, `computer_drag`, `computer_move_mouse` |\n| Act on controls | `computer_invoke`, `compu"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"ter_set_value`, `computer_focus` |\n| Windows | `computer_activate_window`, `computer_move_window`, `"},{"id":"p23s5","text":"computer_close_window` |\n| Timing | `computer_wait` — sleep, or wait until a window / element / titl"},{"id":"p23s6","text":"e substring appears |\n| Runtime | `computer_doctor`, `computer_browser` (read-only CDP list), `compu"},{"id":"p23s7","text":"ter_set_mode` |\n| Wrap-up | `computer_stop` — close the pill and end the takeover (approval kept; `h"},{"id":"p23s8","text":"ard: true` is a real stop) |"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Element ids look like `h=<hwnd>|r=<Role>|n=<Name>|i=<nth>|a=<autoId>`. They are resolved again on ev"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"ery\naction, so a locator from a stale snapshot errors instead of hitting whatever moved under it. `a"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"=` is the\ncontrol automation id and outranks the occurrence index, which drifts between a shallow sn"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"apshot and a deeper walk."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## How it shows up in DSH"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"- The plugin inventory shows **Computer Use** with a blue cursor icon (`locale/en.json`, `package.js"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"on.icon`).\n- The slash menu shows `[hollow cursor] 电脑操作 computer · 批准或撤销电脑操作`. The label and glyph a"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"re\ndecorated client-side: the Host command schema only accepts `name` / `description`, and icons plu"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"s localized\nlabels live in a private client table, so a plugin cannot declare them.\n- The settings c"},{"id":"p26s5","text":"ard lives at Settings → Computer Use."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Settings"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"This card writes the plugin entry Config (all fields hot-reloadable)."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"| Field | Default | What it does |"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"| `mode` | `manual` | `disabled` refuses everything; `readonly` allows observation only; `manual` ne"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"eds `/computer`; `auto` lets the model act freely |\n| `ai_can_change_mode` | `false` | Whether `comp"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"uter_set_mode` may switch modes on its own |\n| `screenshot_dir` | empty | Output directory for scree"},{"id":"p30s4","text":"nshots (empty = OS temp) |\n| `default_scale` | `1` | Default screenshot downscale, 0.1–1 |\n| `typing"},{"id":"p30s5","text":"_interval_ms` | `0` | Delay between characters while typing |\n| `scroll_units` | `1` | Wheel notches"},{"id":"p30s6","text":" per `computer_scroll` (120 WHEEL delta each) |\n| `output_guard` | `true` | Strips fake tool-call/XM"},{"id":"p30s7","text":"L text written as conversation; same text passes on the second output |\n| `debug` | `false` | Logs t"},{"id":"p30s8","text":"he PowerShell script paths |\n| `tool_mode` | `all` | `all` / `lite` / `custom` |\n| `enabled_tools` |"},{"id":"p30s9","text":" `[]` | Allow-list used with `custom` (empty = all) |\n| `stop_hotkey` | `ctrl+alt+esc` | Key shown o"},{"id":"p30s10","text":"n the pill; the pill button always works |\n| `takeover_minutes` | `30` | The pill auto-dismisses (an"},{"id":"p30s11","text":"d stops) after this long; `0` never auto-dismisses |\n| `takeover_message` | empty | Pill title; `{ke"},{"id":"p30s12","text":"y}` is replaced with the hotkey |\n| `cdp_port` | `0` | Chromium `--remote-debugging-port` for `compu"},{"id":"p30s13","text":"ter_browser` (`0` = off) |\n| `approve_observe` | `false` | When on, screenshots / UIA snapshots / wi"},{"id":"p30s14","text":"ndow lists also need `/computer` in `manual` |"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"## Safety model"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"- **Modes.** `disabled` / `readonly` / `manual` / `auto`. Observation tools stay available in `reado"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"disabled` / `readonly` / `manual` / `auto`. Observation tools stay available in `readonly`.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"The host half registers tools and reads its own Config entry; the browser half (`client.js`) renders"},{"id":"p35s2","text":" the\nsettings card through `ctx.configForms` and the official settings-form vocabulary."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"| DSH | Status |"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"| 0.2.0-rc.1 … 0.2.2-alpha.2 | Supported; the version gate is `@deepseek-ai/dsh-settings >=0.1.0-rc."},{"id":"p38s2","text":"6 <0.3.0-0` |\n| 0.1.0-rc.6 … 0.1.7-rc.2 | Supported through the 0.1.x namespaced settings scope |\n| "},{"id":"p38s3","text":"0.3.0 and later | Out of range until verified against that kernel |"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"Windows 10/11 x64. The screenshots and UIA paths were verified on Windows PowerShell 5.1."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
